A||N||11||dnixon||Value of 87 GT||||1
Z||000000||dnixon||11-14-1999||06:23 PM||||My 87 GT was stolen.   I anticipate problems with reimbursement from insurer.   Can anyone tell me what 87 GTs were sold for recently?   It was 80k miles and very clean.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||11-14-1999||07:00 PM||||Sorry about your loss. That really SUX. I bought my 87 GT back in April and it had 122,000 and I paid $2999.00, but the book vaule was $4500.00. Good luck to you, hope you get it back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||11-14-1999||07:31 PM||||Back in April, I bought my 87GT for $5500.  It was extremely clean and it has a few mods to it. It had 83,000 miles on it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||superXmotorsports||11-14-1999||08:52 PM||||I bought a 87 GT last month, 112k miles for $2800.  I sold a 87 GT last year, 56k miles for $5500.  ||||reg||2
Z||000004||87FieroGT||11-14-1999||11:37 PM||||I got my 87 GT for $2700 with only 65,000 miles on it a couple of months back. Have not regreted it since. Should have pictures up on the net soon. To bad yours got stolen I hope you get it back.||||reg||12
Z||000005||87GT||11-14-1999||11:48 PM||||That is a awesome price for one with only 60,000 or so miles on it.  Good for you!||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||11-16-1999||02:08 AM||||Insurance companies like to have car values in writing, when calculating a loss.  Go to <A HREF="http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/</A>  <BR>and click on fiero value. Print it out and<BR>give it to you agent.  It is a little better<BR>than the guide at fiero.net<P>Ross<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||dnixon||11-16-1999||03:32 AM||||To Gokart, 87GT, superXmotorsports, 87FieroGT, RossT and anyone else who may have posted since I read the above.<P>Many thanks for your help.   I do appreciate it.   I have learned lots from your messages.<P>The car hasn't surfaced yet, but I'm still hoping it was just a joy ride and it will be found.<P>I assume all prices quoted were in US dollars.   If any were Canadian can you let me know, please?<P>I'll let you know of the results.<P>dnixon||||reg||1
Z||000008||RFMike||11-16-1999||11:17 PM||||The value of an 87 GT?  Priceless.||||reg||1
Z||000009||dnixon||11-17-1999||02:46 AM||||Thanks RFMike.   I feel that way, too, sometimes.<P>And to everybody else who replied, thanks again.   I got it out of a pound tonight.   Ridden downtown and dumped in a no parking zone a week ago.   Cops only just traced it.   There's no damage at all!   Looks like I'll be getting a kill-switch.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000010||RFMike||11-17-1999||07:13 AM||||Congrats!  That has got to make your day!<BR>Just to let you guys know, this is a very easy car to get into.  I locked my keys in the car about a month ago (first time in about ten years), and it took me about one minute to get in.  Any car with a window that does not slide into a channel is prone to this method- force the window out, slide a rod with a 45 degree bend in it, and slide the lock, or hit the power lock button.  I don't think I'm telling any car thieves anything they don't already know, just giving it out for those who may not have an extra key with them.||||reg||14
Z||000011||DJRice||11-17-1999||08:29 AM||||Your pretty lucky, When my buick was stolen (a 1984) they felt the need to completely trash the interior.  They even broke off the power antenna mast so they would have something to burn their cocaine in. (crack maybe)  I know because I found part of the mast with rubber insulation wrapped around one end.  <P>The kicker is, that one of my friends spotted my car at a gas station a block from his apt, called the cops, and they wouldnt respond because the car wasnt abandoned yet.  They didnt want to have to deal with a possible public confrontation or high speed chase.<P>That pissed me off real good. Naturally by the time I got there, (about 10 minutes) the car was gone.<P>||||reg||1
